---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { NIW, FIELDS, DEGREES, TIMELINES, DO, DONT, SERVICES, ADDONS, RETAINER, STEPS } from '../../data/niw';

const title = 'NIW Consulting';
const description =
  'EB-2 National Interest Waiver petition writing and record-building for professionals in any field. My own self-petition was approved; every petition I have worked on since has been approved. Each engagement starts with an individual review of your record, not a template.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="container niw">
    <header class="page-head niw-hero">
      <span class="kicker">NIW Consulting · EB-2 National Interest Waiver</span>
      <h1 class="display h1">I wrote my own EB-2 NIW petition and it was approved. <em>Now I help professionals build and write theirs.</em></h1>
      <p class="lead">
        I work with professionals across all fields, not only technical ones. Every engagement begins with an individual review of your background, because the evidence that carries a petition in your field is not the evidence that carries one in mine. There is no template.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn" href="#inquiry">Book a Consultation</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#pricing">See services and pricing</a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="track-band" aria-labelledby="track-h">
      <p class="track-line" id="track-h">Every petition I have worked on has been approved.</p>
      <p class="track-sub">My own self-petition was approved, and I have since worked with professionals preparing their own.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="who-h">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <span class="kicker">Who this is for</span>
          <h2 class="display h2" id="who-h">Strong career. Record not yet petition-ready.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="niw-two">
        <div class="prose-block">
          <p>Professionals preparing a self-petitioned EB-2 National Interest Waiver, in any discipline. The people I work with have real careers and real accomplishments. What they usually lack is a record that <em>shows</em> those accomplishments the way a petition has to: documented, independent, and legible to a reviewer who has never met them.</p>
          <p>The approach is field-agnostic on purpose. The work is identifying what counts as evidence in <strong>your</strong> field, and that differs substantially across disciplines. A cited paper carries weight for a researcher. A deployed system, a standard adopted, a program that changed an outcome: those carry it elsewhere. Part of the job is knowing which is which.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="field-list">
          <span class="kicker">Fields I have worked with or can work with</span>
          <div class="tags">
            {FIELDS.filter((f) => f !== 'Other').map((f) => <span>{f}</span>)}
            <span>and others</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="review-h">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <span class="kicker">Individual case review</span>
          <h2 class="display h2" id="review-h">The strategy is built from what is actually there.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="prose-block">
        <p>I do not work from templates, and I do not start writing on day one. Each engagement opens with a full review of your background: education, work history, publications, projects, professional standing, and the things you have done that nobody has written down yet. Only then is there a strategy, and it is yours rather than a form with your name in it.</p>
        <p>That review is also where I tell you plainly what is missing. It is better to hear that from me, twelve months before filing, than from a reviewer afterwards.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="scope-h">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <span class="kicker">Scope</span>
          <h2 class="display h2" id="scope-h">What I do, and what I don't.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="compare">
        <div class="compare-col do">
          <span class="kicker">What I do</span>
          <ul>{DO.map((d) => <li>{d}</li>)}</ul>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-col dont">
          <span class="kicker">What I don't</span>
          <ul>{DONT.map((d) => <li>{d}</li>)}</ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="pricing" aria-labelledby="pricing-h">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <span class="kicker">Services and pricing</span>
          <h2 class="display h2" id="pricing-h">Three ways to work together.</h2>
          <p>Prices in US dollars. No payment is taken on this site; every engagement begins with a conversation.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="price-grid">
        {SERVICES.map((s) => (
          <article class:list={['price-card', { featured: s.recommended }]}>
            {s.recommended && <span class="pill pill-accent">Recommended</span>}
            <h3>{s.name}</h3>
            <p class="price">{s.price}</p>
            <ul>{s.includes.map((i) => <li>{i}</li>)}</ul>
            {s.note && <p class="note">{s.note}</p>}
            <a class:list={['btn', { 'btn-ghost': !s.recommended }]} href="#inquiry">Ask about this</a>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="addons">
        <span class="kicker">Add-ons</span>
        <ul>{ADDONS.map((a) => <li><span>{a.name}</span><b>{a.price}</b></li>)}</ul>
      </div>
      <div class="retainer">
        <div>
          <span class="kicker">Separately</span>
          <h3>{RETAINER.name}</h3>
          <p>{RETAINER.who}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="retainer-price">
          <b>{RETAINER.price}</b>
          <span>{RETAINER.terms}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="pricing-note">{NIW.disclaimer}</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="how-h">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <span class="kicker">How it works</span>
          <h2 class="display h2" id="how-h">Five steps, in order.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps">
        {STEPS.map((s, i) => (
          <li>
            <span class="step-n" aria-hidden="true">{i + 1}</span>
            <div>
              <h3>{s.title}</h3>
              <p>{s.body}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="inquiry" aria-labelledby="inquiry-h">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <span class="kicker">Consultation</span>
          <h2 class="display h2" id="inquiry-h">Tell me about your work.</h2>
          <p>A few details so the first conversation starts from your record rather than from zero. I reply personally, usually within two business days.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <form class="inquiry" method="post" action={NIW.formEndpoint} enctype="multipart/form-data">
        <div class="form-grid">
          <div class="field">
            <label for="f-name">Name <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
            <input id="f-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" required maxlength="120" />
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="f-email">Email <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
            <input id="f-email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required maxlength="200" />
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="f-role">Current role <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
            <input id="f-role" name="role" type="text" autocomplete="organization-title" required maxlength="160" placeholder="e.g. Senior Data Scientist" />
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="f-field">Field or discipline <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
            <select id="f-field" name="field" required>
              <option value="" selected disabled>Choose one</option>
              {FIELDS.map((f) => <option value={f}>{f}</option>)}
            </select>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="f-degree">Highest degree <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
            <select id="f-degree" name="degree" required>
              <option value="" selected disabled>Choose one</option>
              {DEGREES.map((d) => <option value={d}>{d}</option>)}
            </select>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="f-timeline">Target filing timeline <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
            <select id="f-timeline" name="timeline" required>
              <option value="" selected disabled>Choose one</option>
              {TIMELINES.map((t) => <option value={t}>{t}</option>)}
            </select>
          </div>
          <div class="field span">
            <label for="f-background">Background and goals <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
            <textarea id="f-background" name="background" rows="7" required maxlength="6000" aria-describedby="bg-help"></textarea>
            <p class="help" id="bg-help">Your work in a few sentences, what you have published or built, and what you hope to file. Rough is fine.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="field span">
            <label for="f-cv">Your CV or résumé <span class="opt">optional, and the most useful thing you can send</span></label>
            <input id="f-cv" name="cv" type="file" accept=".pdf,.doc,.docx,application/pdf,application/msword,application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document" aria-describedby="cv-help" />
            <p class="help" id="cv-help">PDF or Word, up to 10 MB. The detailed version, not the one-page one: I read it before the first conversation, and the strategy comes out of what is in it.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="hp" aria-hidden="true">
            <label for="f-company">Company</label>
            <input id="f-company" name="company" type="text" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
          </div>
        </div>
        {NIW.turnstileSiteKey && <div class="cf-turnstile" data-sitekey={NIW.turnstileSiteKey} data-theme="auto"></div>}
        <div class="form-actions">
          <button class="btn" type="submit">Request Consultation</button>
          <p class="help">Nothing you write or attach here is stored on this site. It goes to my inbox and nowhere else.</p>
        </div>
      </form>
    </section>

    <aside class="disclaimer-band" role="note" aria-label="Disclaimer">
      <p>{NIW.disclaimer}</p>
    </aside>
  </div>

  {NIW.turnstileSiteKey && <script is:inline src="https://challenges.cloudflare.com/turnstile/v0/api.js" async defer></script>}

  <script is:inline>
    // Catch an oversized or wrong-type CV before the upload starts.
    (function () {
      var input = document.getElementById('f-cv');
      var help = document.getElementById('cv-help');
      if (!input || !help) return;
      var original = help.textContent;
      input.addEventListener('change', function () {
        var f = input.files && input.files[0];
        input.setCustomValidity('');
        help.textContent = original;
        help.classList.remove('is-error');
        if (!f) return;
        var ok = /\.(pdf|docx?)$/i.test(f.name);
        var msg = !ok ? 'That file is not a PDF or Word document.' : f.size > 10 * 1024 * 1024 ? 'That file is larger than 10 MB. Please export a smaller PDF.' : '';
        if (msg) { input.setCustomValidity(msg); help.textContent = msg; help.classList.add('is-error'); }
        else { help.textContent = f.name + ' (' + (f.size / 1024 / 1024).toFixed(1) + ' MB) is ready to send.'; }
      });
    })();
  </script>
</Base>
